<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- This URDF was automatically created by SolidWorks to URDF Exporter! Originally created by Stephen Brawner (brawner@gmail.com)
     Commit Version: 1.6.0-4-g7f85cfe  Build Version: 1.6.7995.38578
     For more information, please see http://wiki.ros.org/sw_urdf_exporter -->
<!--
  Merged with the loone_asv control-layer draft. Real vehicle layout (per team
  description, corrects earlier guesses in this file's history):
    * Twin-float catamaran. base_link is the main body/deck, real CAD data
      from SolidWorks (see urdf/le1000_urdf_t4.csv for the exporter's raw
      dump), sitting between the two floats. The floats themselves are not
      modeled as separate links - they're baked into the base_link.stl mesh
      (see meshes/base_link.stl, shipped as a package asset and used
      directly as base_link's own visual/collision geometry below), so no
      float_l_link/float_r_link are defined here.
    * EACH float has its own propeller and its own rudder (4 actuated joints
      total, not a single shared unit).
    * The exported "Joint1"/"Joint2" meshed links ARE the two real rudders
      (SW component names "Fishtail rudder-1/2" were accurate after all) -
      one per float. Renamed below to rudder_l_link/rudder_r_link.
    * propeller_l_link/propeller_r_link have no CAD mesh yet, so they're
      placeholder primitives, but their positions below are real team
      measurements cross-checked against the full boat mesh
      (meshes/base_link.stl). That mesh has no separate rudder or camera
      parts (assembly stand-ins only) but does include the floats and
      propellers baked into one static shape, which is what the cross-check
      below is based on:
        - float_x (0.20955 m) = the real rudder mount X; the mesh confirms
          each float is centered on that same X. float_height/
          float_end_height (0.259 / 0.122 m, the tapered section that gives
          the propeller clearance) are team measurements, kept only to
          derive prop_z/rudder_mount_z/cam_top_z below - the float bodies
          they describe aren't drawn as separate links anymore.
        - float_z = 0 (the main float box vertically centered on
          base_link's own origin) is inferred, not measured directly - but
          it makes the derived camera top (via head_to_float_top below)
          land within 2 mm of the mesh's true topmost point (Z =
          0.477), so it's a well cross-checked placeholder.
        - propeller Y (0.374 m) and the raw propeller Z reading (-0.173 m,
          kept as prop_z_measured) come directly from the mesh's
          propeller-hub region. Independently, the team's "top of rudder to
          middle of propeller = 0.198 m" measurement matches the straight-
          line distance between the mesh's rudder-top point and this
          propeller position to within 2%.
        - prop_z itself is then moved up from that raw reading to sit flush
          against the float's tapered underside (float_tapered_bottom_z
          minus the propeller radius) instead of hanging below it with a
          visible gap. rudder_mount_z gets the exact same upward shift
          (rudder_z_shift) applied to its real CAD Z (rudder_mount_z_measured),
          so the measured 0.198 m rudder-to-propeller relationship is
          preserved even though both moved.
      TODO(team): replace the propeller placeholder with real per-part
      geometry once the rudder/camera/propeller are modeled as separate
      CAD parts (they're currently only assemblies inside base_link.STL).
    * Two ZED X cameras sit fixed directly on top of the main body
      (base_link), not on the rudder meshes and not on any mast. Body box
      sized from the ZED X spec sheet (164 x 32 x 37 mm, 120 mm stereo
      baseline); swap in zedx_mini_size below if a mount actually uses the
      smaller ZED X variant (94 x 32 x 37 mm, 50 mm baseline). The stereo
      baseline is internal to the camera housing and isn't modeled
      separately.
    * The two cameras face opposite directions (e.g. front/rear coverage),
      cam_span = 0.246 m apart measured face-to-face including the camera
      bodies themselves (per team measurement) - modeled here as a
      front/rear pair along Y, each rotated 180 deg in yaw from the other.
      Vertical placement is derived from a second team measurement: 0.349 m
      from the top of the camera ("top of the head") down to the top of a
      float - see float_z note above for how well that lines up with the
      real mesh.
    * Left/right assignment (J1 => left, J2 => right) is an unverified
      guess. Swap the _l/_r suffixes below if backwards.

  ros2_control interface note: propeller_l_joint/propeller_r_joint use the
  "position" interface even though they're `continuous` - the commanded
  value is a normalized [0,1] thrust fraction sent to a PCA9685 servo/ESC
  channel, not a real angle. rudder_l_joint/rudder_r_joint use real radians.
-->
<robot
   xmlns:xacro="http://wiki.ros.org/xacro" name="loone_asv">

  <material name="hull_grey"><color rgba="0.3 0.3 0.35 1.0"/></material>
  <material name="dark_trim"><color rgba="0.1 0.1 0.1 1.0"/></material>

  <!-- Float layout: centerline X from the real rudder mount (mesh-confirmed). Floats
       aren't drawn as separate links (baked into base_link.stl) - these dimensions are
       kept only to derive prop_z/rudder_mount_z/cam_top_z below. -->
  <xacro:property name="float_x" value="0.20955"/>
  <xacro:property name="float_height" value="0"/>
  <xacro:property name="float_end_height" value="0.122"/>
  <!-- Inferred (not directly measured) - see top-of-file note for the cross-check. -->
  <xacro:property name="float_z" value="0"/>
  <xacro:property name="float_top_z" value="${float_z + float_height / 2}"/>

  <!-- Propeller hub position: Y is from the base_link.STL mesh (see top-of-file note).
       Z is tucked flush against the float's tapered underside instead of the raw mesh
       reading (prop_z_measured), which left a visible gap between propeller and float.
       The same delta is then applied to the rudder mount below so the real measured
       0.198 m top-of-rudder-to-propeller relationship is preserved, not just the
       propeller moved in isolation. -->
  <xacro:property name="propeller_radius" value="0.05"/>
  <xacro:property name="prop_y" value="0.374"/>
  <xacro:property name="prop_z_measured" value="-0.173"/>
  <xacro:property name="float_tapered_bottom_z" value="${float_top_z - float_end_height}"/>
  <xacro:property name="prop_z" value="${float_tapered_bottom_z - propeller_radius}"/>
  <xacro:property name="rudder_z_shift" value="${prop_z - prop_z_measured}"/>
  <!-- Real CAD mount Z from the SolidWorks export, plus the same shift as the propeller above. -->
  <xacro:property name="rudder_mount_z_measured" value="-0.06586"/>
  <xacro:property name="rudder_mount_z" value="${rudder_mount_z_measured + rudder_z_shift}"/>

  <!-- ZED X body box, from the spec sheet (length x depth x height). -->
  <xacro:property name="zedx_length" value="0.164"/>
  <xacro:property name="zedx_depth" value="0.032"/>
  <xacro:property name="zedx_height" value="0.037"/>
  <xacro:property name="zedx_size" value="${zedx_length} ${zedx_depth} ${zedx_height}"/>
  <xacro:property name="zedx_mini_size" value="0.094 0.032 0.037"/>

  <!-- Cameras face opposite directions along Y; span is face-to-face including
       the camera bodies (team measurement), so each box center sits half a
       camera-depth in from the outer face. -->
  <xacro:property name="cam_span" value="0.246"/>
  <xacro:property name="cam_y" value="${(cam_span - zedx_depth) / 2}"/>
  <!-- Vertical placement chains off float_top_z above (team measurement). -->
  <xacro:property name="head_to_float_top" value="0.350"/>
  <xacro:property name="cam_top_z" value="${float_top_z + head_to_float_top}"/>
  <xacro:property name="cam_z" value="${cam_top_z - zedx_height / 2}"/>

  <xacro:macro name="zedx_body">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0" />
      <geometry>
        <box size="${zedx_size}" />
      </geometry>
      <material name="dark_trim"/>
    </visual>
  </xacro:macro>

  <link
    name="base_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin
        xyz="0.0020604 0.014038 0.04597"
        rpy="0 0 0" />
      <mass
        value="15.687" />
      <inertia
        ixx="0.472"
        ixy="-5.4685E-05"
        ixz="-2.1797E-05"
        iyy="0.39383"
        iyz="0.018476"
        izz="0.7806" />
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin
        xyz="0 0 0"
        rpy="0 0 0" />
      <geometry>
        <mesh
          filename="package://le1000_urdf_t4/meshes/base_link.stl"/>
      </geometry>
      <material
        name="hull_grey"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin
        xyz="0 0 0"
        rpy="0 0 0" />
      <geometry>
        <mesh
          filename="package://le1000_urdf_t4/meshes/base_link.stl" />
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <!-- ============================ Rudders (real CAD, one per float) ============================ -->
  <link
    name="rudder_l_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin
        xyz="0.024664 -0.068179 6.8383E-08"
        rpy="0 0 0" />
      <mass
        value="0.16562" />
      <inertia
        ixx="0.00061806"
        ixy="6.8728E-06"
        ixz="2.0765E-09"
        iyy="5.1737E-05"
        iyz="2.5949E-09"
        izz="0.0006647" />
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin
        xyz="0 0 0"
        rpy="0 0 0" />
      <geometry>
        <mesh
          filename="package://le1000_urdf_t4/meshes/Joint1.STL" />
      </geometry>
      <material
        name="dark_trim"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin
        xyz="0 0 0"
        rpy="0 0 0" />
      <geometry>
        <mesh
          filename="package://le1000_urdf_t4/meshes/Joint1.STL" />
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <joint
    name="rudder_l_joint"
    type="revolute">
    <origin
      xyz="0.20955 0.47374 ${rudder_mount_z}"
      rpy="1.5708 0 1.5708" />
    <parent
      link="base_link" />
    <child
      link="rudder_l_link" />
    <axis
      xyz="0 -1 0" />
    <!-- TODO(team): placeholder range; confirm against the real servo/linkage throw. -->
    <limit
      lower="-0.6"
      upper="0.6"
      effort="5.0"
      velocity="3.0" />
  </joint>

  <link
    name="rudder_r_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin
        xyz="0.024664 -0.068179 6.8394E-08"
        rpy="0 0 0" />
      <mass
        value="0.16562" />
      <inertia
        ixx="0.00061806"
        ixy="6.8728E-06"
        ixz="2.0764E-09"
        iyy="5.1737E-05"
        iyz="2.5951E-09"
        izz="0.0006647" />
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin
        xyz="0 0 0"
        rpy="0 0 0" />
      <geometry>
        <mesh
          filename="package://le1000_urdf_t4/meshes/Joint2.STL" />
      </geometry>
      <material
        name="dark_trim"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin
        xyz="0 0 0"
        rpy="0 0 0" />
      <geometry>
        <mesh
          filename="package://le1000_urdf_t4/meshes/Joint2.STL"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <joint
    name="rudder_r_joint"
    type="revolute">
    <origin
      xyz="-0.20955 0.47374 ${rudder_mount_z}"
      rpy="1.5708 0 1.5708" />
    <parent
      link="base_link" />
    <child
      link="rudder_r_link" />
    <axis
      xyz="0 -1 0" />
    <limit
      lower="-0.6"
      upper="0.6"
      effort="5.0"
      velocity="3.0" />
  </joint>

  <!-- ============================ Propellers (placeholder shape, mesh-derived position) ============================ -->
  <!-- Modeled as `continuous` so ros2_control can expose a command interface; the
       numeric command is a normalized [0,1] thrust fraction, NOT a real angle. -->
  <link name="propeller_l_link"><visual><geometry><cylinder radius="${propeller_radius}" length="0.08"/></geometry><material name="dark_trim"/></visual></link>
  <link name="propeller_r_link"><visual><geometry><cylinder radius="${propeller_radius}" length="0.08"/></geometry><material name="dark_trim"/></visual></link>

  <joint name="propeller_l_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="propeller_l_link"/>
    <origin xyz="${float_x} ${prop_y} ${prop_z}" rpy="0 1.5708 1.5708"/>
    <axis xyz="0 0 1"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="propeller_r_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="propeller_r_link"/>
    <origin xyz="${-float_x} ${prop_y} ${prop_z}" rpy="0 1.5708 1.5708"/>
    <axis xyz="0 0 1"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ============================ Cameras (fixed on top of main body) ============================ -->
  <link name="cam_1_link">
    <xacro:zedx_body/>
  </link>
  <link name="cam_2_link">
    <xacro:zedx_body/>
  </link>

  <!-- Boresight (local +X) must point along the hull's actual fore-aft axis, which
       is Y here (bow at -Y, stern at +Y; see propeller_l/r_joint and
       rudder_l/r_joint, both further out on +Y). A yaw of 0/180 only swings the
       boresight between +X/-X (port/starboard), so both joints below carry an
       extra +/-90 deg on top of the front/rear 180 deg split to actually aim
       outward along Y instead of sideways. -->
  <joint name="cam_1_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="cam_1_link"/>
    <!-- Stern side (same side as props/rudder): boresight faces +Y (aft). -->
    <origin xyz="0 ${cam_y} ${cam_z}" rpy="0 0 1.5708"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="cam_2_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="cam_2_link"/>
    <!-- Bow side, confirmed physical front camera: boresight faces -Y (forward). -->
    <origin xyz="0 ${-cam_y} ${cam_z}" rpy="0 0 -1.5708"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ============================ ros2_control ============================ -->
  <!--
    Stock topic_based_ros2_control hardware: it bridges the command/state interfaces
    below to plain ROS topics instead of a real driver, so the actual PCA9685 access
    can live in a Python driver node (no C++) subscribed to joint_commands_topic and
    publishing joint_states_topic.
  -->
  <ros2_control name="asv" type="system">
    <hardware>
      <plugin>topic_based_ros2_control/TopicBasedSystem</plugin>
      <param name="joint_commands_topic">/asv/joint_commands</param>
      <param name="joint_states_topic">/asv/joint_states</param>
    </hardware>

    <joint name="propeller_l_joint">
      <command_interface name="position"/>
      <state_interface name="position"/>
    </joint>
    <joint name="propeller_r_joint">
      <command_interface name="position"/>
      <state_interface name="position"/>
    </joint>
    <joint name="rudder_l_joint">
      <command_interface name="position"/>
      <state_interface name="position"/>
    </joint>
    <joint name="rudder_r_joint">
      <command_interface name="position"/>
      <state_interface name="position"/>
    </joint>
  </ros2_control>

</robot>
